## 5. Metrics
Bias, SD, RMSE of (τ̂−τ)/τ; RMSE ratio to DM (paired draws; CI by paired two-level bootstrap: graph draws, then assignments within graph, same indices
for both estimators); sign-error rate P(τ̂ < 0); 95 % CI coverage and mean width (normal CI with HC0 / bootstrap SE);
measured DM bias per cell. Uncertainty of every cell metric: two-level bootstrap over graph draws and assignments (assignments only on fixed real graphs; 2000 resamples).
Pooled statements across cells (R², regime boundaries) resample at the mechanism / graph-family level (§6).

## 6. Diagnostic test (P5, C6) and the acceptance rule — copied from the Brief, fixed
Quantities per replicate, from stored data: leverage L = n‖w_chin‖²; S = RMS deviation of the other ladder specifications
(quad, spline, count, hop2) from `chin`, recomputed at each noise level m from sig + m·sd·nz; S′ = SD among the others only;
raw corner distances 1−mean f and mean f, and distance outside the support 1−max f, min f; curvature ĝ'' = 2·(quad f² coefficient).
* Part (i), variance: across cells and graph draws, R² of log realised variance on log L (+ log n, log σ²), against benchmarks;
  departure ratio realised/(σ²L/n).
* Part (ii), bias: |realised bias| per cell vs S̄ (computed on a random half of the draws, bias on the other half) and corner distance × estimated curvature.
* Within-cell test (S and bootstrap SE only): Spearman of S with |centred error|, minus the same statistic from a **null simulation**
  (outcomes generated from the reporting specification itself, correct spec, noise only); if the mechanical part is large S is replaced by S′.
* Combined score: leave-one-mechanism-out and leave-one-graph-family-out R² of log-RMSE of the combined score vs each benchmark: mean degree,
  p(1−p), n·p(1−p)/d, the bootstrap SE, Han–Ugander-style CV loss (Tier A subset; benchmark compared only on those cells and said so).
* Acceptance (fixed): **Supported** if (1) pooled held-out R² gain over the best benchmark ≥ 0.05 with group-level bootstrap CI excluding 0,
  (2) gain positive in ≥ 4 of 6 held-out mechanisms and survives deleting any single group, (3) part (i) beats its benchmarks on realised variance and part (ii) on |realised bias|,
  (4) the within-cell excess over the null simulation has median CI above 0 and above that of the bootstrap SE. **Inconclusive** if the point gain ≥ 0.05 but the group-level CI includes 0.
  Otherwise **not supported** and the reason is analysed.
* "Regression beats DM below a spillover threshold": stated with the oracle s (known) and with ŝ = estimated spillover share = (τ̂_chin − β̂_z)/τ̂_chin from the same regression.
  The regime map's flip contour is estimated from the (s, mechanism) grid by interpolating log RMSE-ratio over s.

## 7. Known departures from the Brief (to be settled with `idea-repo`)
* Causal message passing (Shirani & Bayati 2024) is defined for sequential/panel outcomes; the experiment here has one outcome per unit, so it cannot be run as published — to be reported to `idea-repo` for a substitute.
* Tier A (selection by cross-validation with graph-cluster folds + corner loss; lasso/ridge/forest/boosting; optional GNN) runs on a subset of ≈30 cells, ≈100 draws, in a separate stage (`src/gate/tierA.py`), after the Tier-G results are in. Adaptive-threshold HT (Thiyageswaran et al.) is run only if the published rule is available and specifiable.
* Louvain γ rule: three fixed resolutions on every graph; there is no tuned rule.
* Noise draws: one per assignment (not nested), the conditional noise variance being known exactly; graph-draw and assignment-draw variation are nested.

